// A `move` TAKES AN OWNING PLACE (DEF-416, landing 177b; `NITPICK-TYPE-104`, `move_path_verdict` in type_stmt.npk, judged after the function's walk). A `move` whose place reaches its
// value through a PLAIN pointer, a handle or a view -- `move(p.s)`, `move((<-p).s)`, `move(<-p)`, `move(h.items[i])` through `Holder->:h`, a slice local of a local, a `Self->` receiver's
// field, a generic `T` behind a pointer, a pick arm's or a struct literal's `move(p.s)` -- leaves the pointee's owner reading a slot VACATED where no rule judged the owner (p7_through_holder 60 on 175, 176b and 177a: the
// owner's length read 0; lo_ptr_move 65 and m1 65 are `t.len + 60`, q1 70 its program's own sum -- the pointee is moved out and left vacant, D-225, no copy and no
// double free: management_13's cells rc2c, ra2c, rc2a of 2026-11-01, build 8's correction of this line), or a store after the move that drops freed bytes (q1_store_after_move, q4_by_callee, q6_copy_order,
// q7_init_order: management_13's cells, 2026-11-01). THE ROAD OUT OF A POINTEE is the DECLARED-UNCHECKED one: `move((<-(p =>! wild T->)).s)` (the cast asserts the pointee is the author's, D-019;
// m14/m14b run right) or a `wild`-qualified slot, judged by ORIGIN -- a wild pointer or `#wild_slice` local whose address is this frame's (`@local` stored into it, a re-pointed wild local: m13,
// q9, q10, r416b_wild_local_root, r416c_wild_derived) is refused, one from a parameter, a global, `NULL`, `alloc` or `#ptr_add` is not. A `pass` of such a place is the same refusal on the pass
// road, `NITPICK-TYPE-047` (m11, r416_pass_deref, r416b_pass_*, r416b_call_deref, r416b_local_ptr, r416c_return_lit; r416b_return_lit's TYPE-037 is 177a's). The copy-typed element and field
// are exempt (a copy is no move: m7, k1). OVER-REFUSED ON PURPOSE, THE POST-180 LIST: `k2_realloc_field_ok` (a bare `alloc` call's result in a field, not read by `ptr_from_outside`) and
// `q11_wild_slice_copy_ok` (a `#wild_slice` copied into a second plain slice local); management_13's ruling of 16:57 EST. [DATED 2026-11-01 18:28 EST, build 7: `k2_realloc_field_ok` is LEGAL now, in the `_ok`;
// the bare `alloc` call is read as an origin (the omission below); `q11` stays on the post-180 list.] The legal twins are `tests/backend/programs/move_through_pointer_ok.npk`.
// The cells: `.internal/probes177b/cells416*/` (the seat's grid and probes), `MANAGEMENT/probes/177b-def416/` (management_13's); the results `.internal/probes177b/out_b6/`.
// ADDED AT management_13's RULING OF 17:59:32 EST: the twelve attempts to launder a frame's own address through `src/`'s inline road, `move((<-(X =>! wild H->)).s)` with X an `@h`, a copy of
// it, a wild local of it, a field's address, a call given `@h`, `any->` first, a ternary with an `@h` arm, a holder's field, a parameter re-pointed before the move and one re-pointed after it in a
// loop (`i1`-`i12`: ten TYPE-104; `i4_cast_param_ok` and `i5_cast_copy_of_param`, a plain parameter or a copy of it with the slot restored, legal, in the `_ok`); and the LOCK's old spellings of
// `tests/analysis/rejection/spawn_lends.npk` (landing 173 to 177a, BORROW-001 by DEF-393(a)'s `lends` mark then): `pass move(<-sp)` after a spawn stored a frame borrow into the lock is TYPE-104
// (`lk1`), `pass <-sp` TYPE-047 (`lk2`); the BY-VALUE `pass move(v)` of that lock is accepted today, DEF-395's face 1 (landing 179), parked whole in `tests/parked/def395-by-value/`.
// ADDED AFTER CHAIN 1 (build 7, 18:28 EST): the walk had two omissions, found by the tree's own emission -- a bare `alloc`/`ralloc`/`aalloc` call or a user
// allocator declaring a wild return was not an ORIGIN (`ptr_from_outside` read the sigil form alone), and a builtin's or a call's result at the END of a path
// was walked on and refused as unplaceable -- so it refused the manual regime's own pattern (tests/backend/programs/deref_store_drop.npk's case 9, `move(<-ws)`
// over `ws = m =>! wild string->`, `m = alloc(...)`) and lib/ntensor.npk's `get` (`pass (<-(#ptr_add<T>(self.cells.ptr, off)))`). Both fixed in build 7; the
// legal cells `pa1`, `pa4`, `al1`, `al2`, `al4` are in the `_ok`. Here: `al3`, an own address laundered through a PLAIN call and cast wild, stays TYPE-104
// (the call is not seen through, the closed direction); `rl1`, the long form `return Result{value: <-pa}` over a pointer parameter, TYPE-047 (the pass
// road; tests/backend/programs/result_literal_road_ok.npk's control 13 from landing 171 to 177a, retired there).
// ADDED AT management_13's RULING OF 18:42:35 EST (the cap 135 at base; its second attempt to launder through F1 and F2, on build 7, `MANAGEMENT/probes/177b-def416/`,
// README's last table; the seat's run `.internal/probes177b/cells8.txt`, 177a → build 7): a block from `alloc` RE-POINTED to `@o` before the move (`al5`, 65 on 177a), a user
// allocator's cell re-pointed after the move in a loop (`al6`, 70) and through a copy (`al7`, 70); `#ptr_add` over `@arr[0]` held and inline (`pa5`, `pa6`, 65), over a LOCAL
// struct's wild field (`pa7`, 65: `v` is no pointer, the closed direction), over a pointer parameter's field re-pointed to `@o` before and after the move (`pa9`, `pa10`,
// BORROW-002 on 177a): TYPE-104; the pass road over own storage (`pa11`, BORROW-001 on 177a): TYPE-047. Legal, in the `_ok`: `u4` (a user allocator's cell), `pa8` (a
// parameter's wild field under `#ptr_add`), `pa12` (the pass road over it). ACCEPTED, 65 on 177a and here, IN NEITHER TEST BY THE RULING: `u1`-`u3`,
// `func:lie = wild string->(string->:q) { pass (q =>! wild string->); }` with `move(<-(raw lie(@o)))` -- the one trust F1 adds, the callee's own explicit `=>!`, the
// assertion `i4` makes on a plain parameter (D-095); DEF-416's row names them, so nobody reads the road as closed.
// ADDED AT management_13's RULING OF 01:21:29 EST (the amend of build 9; its cells `MANAGEMENT/probes/177b-b9/`): `rk7a`-`rk7c`, a frame address `@h` in each VALUE position
// after two turbofish types (60 on 177a, the owner read vacant): TYPE-104 -- the pins of the call arm's walk over the VALUE arguments alone; its legal side, a block from
// `alloc` at that position (`rk7t`), stands in the standalone `tests/backend/programs/generic_call_window_ok.npk`, the pin of the turbofish fix (build 8 refused both).
mod:move_through_pointer;
